## Architecture

### Data Structure

Tree data as nested JavaScript object. Each node has:

```javascript
{
  id: "unique-id",           // kebab-case, globally unique
  name: "Display Name",      // bold title in the node box
  subtitle: "secondary text", // smaller text below name
  detail: "tertiary info",   // even smaller, dimmed
  type: "standard",          // determines border color
  children: [...]            // optional, nested nodes
}
```

### Node Types and Colors

```javascript
const TYPE_COLORS = {
  'standard':     '#38bdf8',  // blue - default
  'mce':          '#f472b6',  // pink - platform layer
  'framework':    '#4ade80',  // green - active reconciler/controller
  'spoke':        '#fbbf24',  // amber - runs on managed cluster
  'user-creates': '#a78bfa',  // purple - user-created resource
  'dim':          '#7a84a0',  // gray - de-emphasized
};
```

Add custom types as needed for domain-specific coloring.

### Side Panel Data

Separate `DATA` object mapping node IDs to panel content:

```javascript
const DATA = {
  'node-id': {
    title: 'Panel Title',
    html: `<div class="detail-section">
      <h4>Section Header</h4>
      <div class="value">Description text</div>
      <pre class="data-block">key: value</pre>
    </div>`
  },
  // ...
};
```

For generic patterns (e.g., ReplicaSet/Pod nodes), use ID suffix matching in `showDetail()`:

```javascript
if (nodeId.endsWith('-rs')) { /* generic ReplicaSet panel */ }
else if (nodeId.endsWith('-pods')) { /* generic Pod panel */ }
```

## Key Features

### 0. Sequential Flow Renderer (for pipelines/workflows)

For sequential data (step-by-step pipelines), use a grid-based flow layout with directional arrows. No expand/collapse -- every node is always visible. Click opens the side panel.

```javascript
function renderFlow(containerId) {
  // Lay out nodes in a snake pattern (L→R, then R→L on next row)
  const cols = 4;
  steps.forEach((step, i) => {
    const col = i % cols;
    const row = Math.floor(i / cols);
    const isReversed = row % 2 === 1;
    step._cx = isReversed ? (cols-1-col) * totalW : col * totalW;
    step._cy = row * totalH;
  });
  // Draw arrows between consecutive steps (horizontal or U-turn)
  // Click on node → showDetail(step.id), NO expand/collapse
}
```

Arrow markers use per-type colors so the flow visually shows which type of component comes next. Snake pattern (boustrophedon) keeps the diagram compact for long pipelines.

### 1. Collapsible Tree (D3.js v7)

```javascript
// Toggle children on click
function toggle(d) {
  if (d.children) {
    d._children = d.children;  // collapse: store in _children
    d.children = null;
  } else {
    d.children = d._children;  // expand: restore from _children
    d._children = null;
  }
  update(d);
}
```

**Critical**: Recursive collapse for deep trees:
```javascript
function collapseAll(node) {
  if (node.children) {
    node._children = node.children;
    node._children.forEach(collapseAll);
    node.children = null;
  }
}
```

### 2. Separate Click Targets

The node body (rect) and expand/collapse button (+/-) must be SEPARATE click targets:

- **Click node body** → opens side panel with details (no expand/collapse)
- **Click +/- button** → toggles expand/collapse (no side panel)

The +/- button is a `<g>` group containing a `<rect>` + `<text>`, positioned inside the top-right corner of the node box. Add hover effects:
- Hovering collapsed (+): green glow → "click to expand"
- Hovering expanded (−): red glow → "click to collapse"

Text labels inside nodes need `pointer-events: none` to prevent intercepting clicks.

### 3. Pan and Zoom

```javascript
const zoomBehavior = d3.zoom()
  .scaleExtent([0.1, 3])
  .on('zoom', (event) => {
    g.attr('transform', event.transform);
    document.getElementById('zoom-pct').textContent = Math.round(event.transform.k * 100) + '%';
  });
svg.call(zoomBehavior);
```

Floating zoom controls: +, -, Reset, Expand All (E+), Collapse All (C-)

### 4. Side Panel

35% width, slides in from right. Sticky header with close button. Contains:
- `<h4>` section headers (accent2 color, uppercase)
- `<div class="value">` description text
- `<pre class="data-block">` for CLI output / key-value data
- `<pre class="yaml-block">` for YAML with toggle buttons
- `<span class="tag tag-xxx">` for colored badges

### 5. Legend

Color-coded legend strip below the diagram showing node type meanings.

### 6. Initial Collapse State

Use `collapseAfterDepth(root, N)` to start with a manageable view:
- Small diagrams (<50 nodes): start fully expanded
- Medium (50-150): collapse after depth 5-7
- Large (150+): collapse after depth 4-6

